//api.github.com/repos/ionic-team/ionic-framework/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ionic-team/ionic-framework/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ionic-team/ionic-framework/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ionic-team/ionic-framework/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ionic-team/ionic-framework/deployments","created_at":"2013-08-20T23:06:02Z","updated_at":"2026-03-10T22:25:53Z","pushed_at":"2026-03-10T18:20:22Z","git_url":"git://github.com/ionic-team/ionic-framework.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:ionic-team/ionic-framework.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/ionic-team/ionic-framework.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/ionic-team/ionic-framework","homepage":"https://ionicframework.com","size":1570981,"stargazers_count":52388,"watchers_count":52388,"language":"TypeScript","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":13388,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":625,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["angular","capacitor","framework","frontend","ionic","ios","javascript","material-design","mobile","pwa","react","stencil","stenciljs","typescript","ui-components","vue","web","webcomponents"],"visibility":"public","forks":13388,"open_issues":625,"watchers":52388,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"#### Short description of the problem:\n\nI was trying to create a roll-up/down component. Angular2 provides animations functionality out-of-the-box that you can attach to your component. For my component, the component animates, however the animation easing is not respected. The animation ease is always linear.\n\nThe component is as follows:\n\n```\nimport {Component, Directive, Input} from '@angular/core';\nimport {trigger, state, style, transition, animate} from '@angular/core'\n\n@Component({\n    selector: 'expandable',\n    templateUrl: `<div *ngIf=\"isExpanded\" @animate=\"'slide'\"><ng-content></ng-content></div>`,\n    animations: [\n        trigger('animate', [\n            state('slide', style({ overflow: 'hidden', height: '*' })),\n            transition('slide => void', [animate('2000ms ease', style({ height: 0 }))]),\n            transition('void => slide', [style({ overflow: 'hidden', height: 0 }), animate('2000ms ease',  style({ height: '*' }))]),\n        ])\n    ]\n})\nexport class SimExpandable {\n    private _expanded: boolean = false;\n    @Input('expanded') set expanded(value: string | boolean) {\n        this._expanded = (value === 'true' || value === true);\n    }\n    get isExpanded(): boolean { return this._expanded }\n}\n```\n\nIt can be used like so:\n\n```\n<button (click)=\"myFlag=!myFlag\">HEADING</button>\n<expandable [expanded]=\"myFlag\">\n    <ion-card>\n        <p>Hello</p>\n        <p>World</p>\n    </ion-card>\n</expandable>\n```\n\nI've created an [Angular 2 Plunkr](http://plnkr.co/edit/yS4ksXpXQekLfLlJPZKf?p=preview) and the animation works fine there. I haven't been able to create a corresponding an Ionic 2 Plunkr as the plunkr reports all of the symbols in the following line are `undefined`:\n\n`import { trigger, state, style, transition, animate } from '@angular/core'`\n#### What behavior are you expecting?\n\nLike the [Angular 2 Plunkr](http://plnkr.co/edit/yS4ksXpXQekLfLlJPZKf?p=preview), I'd expect that the animation ease mentioned should be respected, and not always linear.\n\n**Steps to reproduce:**\n1. Create a blank application. \n2. Add the component TS listed above.\n3. Use the component as listed in code above.\n4. Run the application and try clicking the button. The `div` should roll-up/down starting slowly, speeding up and then stopping slowly as well. It doesn't for me and the entire motion is at constant speed. Compare it to the [Angular 2 Plunkr](http://plnkr.co/edit/yS4ksXpXQekLfLlJPZKf?p=preview) and you'll see the difference.\n\n**Which Ionic Version?** 1.x or 2.x\n\nI'm using 2.x. I've tried both `angular-ionic@beta` and `angular-ionic@nightly`.\n#### Plunker that shows an example of your issue\n\nhttp://plnkr.co/edit/yS4ksXpXQekLfLlJPZKf?p=preview\n\n**Run `ionic info` from terminal/cmd prompt:** (paste output below)\n\n**My application**\nCordova CLI: 6.1.1\nGulp version:  CLI version 3.9.1\nGulp local:   Local version 3.9.1\nIonic Framework Version: 2.0.0-beta.10-201606302045\nIonic CLI Version: 2.0.0-beta.31\nIonic App Lib Version: 2.0.0-beta.17\nios-deploy version: Not installed\nios-sim version: 5.0.8 \nOS: Mac OS X El Capitan\nNode Version: v4.4.2\nXcode version: Xcode 7.3.1 Build version 7D1014 \n\n**My test application**\nCordova CLI: 6.1.1\nGulp version:  CLI version 3.9.1\nGulp local:   Local version 3.9.1\nIonic Framework Version: 2.0.0-beta.10\nIonic CLI Version: 2.0.0-beta.31\nIonic App Lib Version: 2.0.0-beta.17\nios-deploy version: Not installed\nios-sim version: 5.0.8 \nOS: Mac OS X El Capitan\nNode Version: v4.4.2\nXcode version: Xcode 7.3.1 Build version 7D1014 \n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ionic-team/ionic-framework/issues/7240/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ionic-team/ionic-framework/issues/7240/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/comments/529242979","html_url":"https://github.com/angular/angular/issues/9517#issuecomment-529242979","issue_url":"https://api